WEBVTT

00:08:30.246 --> 00:08:31.913
like how many points you score,

00:08:32.204 --> 00:08:35.746
how many steals you make and how
you rebound and so forth.

00:08:36.412 --> 00:08:39.579
And there is some effect
of that, obviously.

00:08:39.746 --> 00:08:45.371
But there's also a very significant effect
of how high you were in the draft.

00:08:45.621 --> 00:08:47.871
Even if top draft picks
weren't playing well,

00:08:48.162 --> 00:08:49.912
coaches still kept them in the game.

00:08:50.829 --> 00:08:52.371
They made a big bet on this guy,

00:08:52.829 --> 00:08:54.996
so they wanted to prove they
made the right decision

00:08:55.204 --> 00:08:58.871
and hadn't blown millions
beyond ego and image.

00:08:58.912 --> 00:09:02.579
There's another emotional factor that
fuels these kinds of escalation traps